    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d619">

                <pb facs="0680" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg668"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Brazil/3380b: Airgram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-10T09:30:00-04:00">May 10, 1943—9:30
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–1416. Embassy at Buenos Aires advises that Argentina imported crude rubber from
                    Brazil in amount of 4 kilos in January, 12,405 in February and 7,648 in March,
                    or a total of 20,057 for the first quarter. Department would like explanation of
                    these shipments in violation of rubber agreement between Brazil and United
                        States.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d619-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d619-f1" n="39" xml:id="d619-f1-content">
                <p>For the Department’s position on this trade, see telegram No. 3012, August 11, to
                    the Ambassador in Brazil, <ref target="#pg674">p. 674</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
